#: backend/dbm_aiagent/mcp_tools/common/views/promql_query.py:80
msgid ""
"按 cluster 来查询集群级别监控指标。根据指标名称、标签过滤条件、聚合方式等参数"
"自动构建 PromQL 并查询监控数据。支持 range_function（Gauge 指标用 max/min/"
"sum/avg/count 对应 *_over_time，Counter 指标用 rate/increase）和外层聚合（如 "
"max/sum/avg 等），以及 group_by 分组。返回时序数据和实际执行的 PromQL 语句。"
msgstr "Press cluster to query cluster-level monitoring indicators. Automatically build PromQL and query monitoring data based on parameters such as indicator name, label filter conditions, aggregation method, etc. Supports range_function (Gauge indicator uses max/min/sum/avg/count corresponding to *_over_time, Counter indicator uses rate/increase) and outer aggregation (such as max/sum/avg, etc.), as well as group_by grouping. Returns time series data and the actual executed PromQL statement."

#: backend/dbm_aiagent/mcp_tools/common/views/promql_query.py:114
msgid ""
"按 cluster instance(ip:port) 来查询实例级别监控指标。根据指标名称、标签过滤条"
"件、聚合方式等参数自动构建 PromQL 并查询监控数据。支持 range_function（Gauge "
"指标用 max/min/sum/avg/count 对应 *_over_time，Counter 指标用 rate/increase）"
"和外层聚合（如 max/sum/avg 等），以及 group_by 分组。返回时序数据和实际执行"
"的 PromQL 语句。"
msgstr "Press cluster instance(ip:port) to query instance-level monitoring indicators. Automatically build PromQL and query monitoring data based on parameters such as indicator name, label filter conditions, aggregation method, etc. Supports range_function (Gauge indicator uses max/min/sum/avg/count corresponding to *_over_time, Counter indicator uses rate/increase) and outer aggregation (such as max/sum/avg, etc.), as well as group_by grouping. Returns time series data and the actual executed PromQL statement."

#: backend/dbm_aiagent/mcp_tools/common/views/resource_param_query.py:40
msgid ""
"Query resource request parameters by bill_id or task_id. This tool retrieves "
"the resource allocation parameters submitted during ticket/task execution, "
"useful for debugging resource issues or auditing resource requests. 根据单据"
"ID(bill_id)或任务ID(task_id)查询资源请求参数。用于获取单据/任务执行时提交的资"
"源申请参数，适用于排查资源问题或审计资源请求。"
msgstr "Query resource request parameters by bill_id or task_id. This tool retrieves the resource allocation parameters submitted during ticket/task execution, useful for debugging resource issues or auditing resource requests. Query resource request parameters by bill ID (bill_id) or task ID (task_id). Used to obtain the resource application parameters submitted when the document/task is executed, suitable for troubleshooting resource problems or auditing resource requests."

